{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.PlanckTime","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.PlanckTime","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planck_length_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planck_length_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.lean#L59-L70","doc":"Planck length is identically 1: `ℏ_q · t_P = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planckTime_eq_inv_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planckTime_eq_inv_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.lean#L48-L57","doc":"Planck time equals the reciprocal of the quantum Planck\nconstant: `t_P = ℏ_q⁻¹`, stated as the inverse of the unit\n`hbarUnit` (whose value is `ℏ_q` by `hbarUnit_val`).  Over a\nfield this is the familiar `planckTime = 1 / (1 - q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarUnit_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarUnit_val","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.lean#L41-L46","doc":"The unit `hbarUnit` really has value `ℏ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarUnit","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.lean#L36-L39","doc":"`ℏ_q` is itself a unit whenever `q - 1` is, namely\n`ℏ_q = q⁻¹ · (q - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planckTime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planckTime","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.lean#L29-L34","doc":"Planck time as a function of the substrate parameter `q`:\n`t_P = q / (q - 1)`, written division-free as `q · (q-1)⁻¹`\nwith `q - 1` supplied as the unit `d`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:planck-time","label":"def:planck-time","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/planck-time.lean#L24-L27","doc":"The quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`, for `q` a unit of\nthe ground ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}